.TH "RUN-DEV-PODMAN.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
run\-dev\-podman.sh \- launch the project development image through Podman
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBrun\-dev\-podman.sh [OPTIONS]\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the published Debian development image as a project\-specific sandbox using the current working directory as /workspace. The launcher chooses a sandbox name, pulls the published image by default, inspects its seeded\-home capability, and sets up project home and workspace storage. It does not mount the host home directory or host container\-engine socket. For supported image layouts, upgrades and auth persistence, see containers/dev\-dotfiles\-debian/README.md in this repository.
.PP
Outer containers are ephemeral by default, while configured named volumes survive container removal. A stopped older persistent container is not silently deleted or replaced. The published image may have changed since the last run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-podman\-security=nested|unconfined|privileged|off\fR
Control support for rootless Podman inside the sandbox. The default is nested; unconfined relaxes AppArmor, privileged grants more access, and off skips nested Podman setup.
.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-container\fR
Keep the outer container after it stops and resume an existing stopped container by name.
.TP
\fB\-\-ephemeral\-container\fR
Remove new outer containers on exit (default). Existing stopped containers are never removed automatically.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-home\-volume\fR
Do not mount the per\-project persistent /home/user volume; requires a home\-seed image.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-workspace\-mount\fR
Do not mount the current working directory into /workspace.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBSANDBOX_NAME\fR
Override the per\-project container name, normally derived from the current directory.
.TP
\fBDEV_IMAGE\fR
Override the default ghcr.io/arran4/dev\-dotfiles\-debian:latest image.
.TP
\fBDEV_PULL_MODE\fR
always, missing or never. Published images default to always; local images default to never.
.TP
\fBDEV_CONTAINER_PERSIST\fR
0 (default) or 1, equivalent to the outer container persistence flags.
.TP
\fBDEV_WORKSPACE_MODE\fR
bind (default), volume or container. A bind mount maps the current directory to /workspace.
.TP
\fBDEV_HOME_MODE\fR
volume (default) or container; the latter needs a seeded image.
.TP
\fBDEV_NEW_HOME\fR
0 (default) or 1. Cannot bypass an existing container or force a legacy image into the seeded layout.
.TP
\fBDEV_PODMAN_SECURITY\fR
nested (default), unconfined, privileged or off.
.TP
\fBDEV_DIND\fR
1 (default) enables Docker\-in\-Docker and makes the outer container privileged. Use 0 to disable this capability.
.TP
\fBDEV_DIND_PERSIST\fR
1 makes Docker\-in\-Docker data persistent (requires DEV_DIND=1).
.TP
\fBDEV_PODMAN_PERSIST\fR
1 mounts a persistent nested\-Podman data volume.
.TP
\fBDEV_TZ\fR
Explicit container time zone; otherwise detected from the host.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cd ~/Documents/Projects/example
run\-dev\-podman.sh
DEV_DIND=0 run\-dev\-podman.sh \-\-podman\-security=off
.fi
.SH NOTES
SECURITY: DEV_DIND=1 is the default and causes the launcher to use a privileged outer container. Do not describe this configuration as a strict sandbox for untrusted code. Review trust boundaries and consider DEV_DIND=0 when nested Docker is not needed.
.PP
Resuming a persistent outer container uses its original image and mounts. Pulling a newer image alone does not upgrade that already\-created container.
.PP
The two launchers use the same image definition, but select their corresponding host container engines.
.SH SEE ALSO
run\-dev\-docker.sh(1)
